{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:9.25.020","page_type":"section"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"3855f65c0c6780c6864bee9f581c67e3458fba410a342662451b0b6d0fd5479e","heading":"Definitions.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Dwelling unit” means a structure or the part of a structure that is used as a home, residence or sleeping place by one person who maintains a household or by two or more persons who maintain a common household.\n“Good faith” means honesty in fact in the conduct of a transaction.\n“Good standing” means that a tenant is not in arrears in the payment of rent and is in compliance with the duties of a tenant enumerated in K.S.A. 58-2555 and amendments thereto.\n“Landlord” means the owner or lessor of a dwelling unit or the building of which the unit is a part.\n“Rental agreement” means all agreements, written or oral, embodying the terms and conditions concerning the use and occupancy of a dwelling unit.\n“Retaliate” or “retaliatory action” shall include but not be limited to any of the following actions by a landlord when such actions penalize a tenant because of an action identified in TMC 9.25.030 :\n(1) Commencement of any action or proceeding to recover possession of a dwelling from a tenant;\n(2) Increasing the rent;\n(3) Reduction of services required to be provided by the landlord pursuant to the rental agreement and/or K.S.A. 58-2553 and amendments thereto; and\n(4) Harassing entry or repeated demands for entry of the tenant’s dwelling unit by the landlord in violation of K.S.A. 58-2557 and/or 58-2571(b)\n“Tenant” means a person entitled under a rental agreement to occupy a dwelling unit. (Ord. 20488 § 2, 5-14-24.)\nCross References: Definitions generally, TMC 1.10.020 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"6d037a5b-d239-559f-97cc-f38e60fbb1ff"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"1811ee4d0977ab5a455d1eef36aa7108364a37b8e92f845ad98ef1a29b688ff8","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Dwelling unit” means a structure or the part of a structure that is used as a home, residence or sleeping place by one person who maintains a household or by two or more persons who maintain a common household.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"26fcf55c-b100-5177-96a1-c6dca04bfb9c"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"51d100cc56b375403c9607d3cd5fe83f09e433cb8dbaddd6cd6e933a5cd09bf8","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Good faith” means honesty in fact in the conduct of a transaction.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"92062a8f-3a59-5224-8612-2de6a4d30298"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"27963bff22e50b8e368fc34d8418a962be988137d0438b0dbf659aeffb74c02a","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Good standing” means that a tenant is not in arrears in the payment of rent and is in compliance with the duties of a tenant enumerated in K.S.A. 58-2555 and amendments thereto.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"f84edae4-5f8c-5a43-acb7-b37e586a0910"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"e21ad16835c919e90a4723bae701556acaa4c891b3894468d1c6331396f94bef","heading":null,"ordinal":3,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:block:3","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Landlord” means the owner or lessor of a dwelling unit or the building of which the unit is a part.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"95e65fd4-cccb-589b-a59d-cb312a8b5abe"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"b49e56420ec93e0dda01439d0d8d04601e908c78c6ab576865b140b8ec274d5c","heading":null,"ordinal":4,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:9.25.020:block:4","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","text":"“Rental agreement” means all agreements, written or oral, embodying the terms and conditions concerning the use and occupancy of a dwelling unit.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"7b502ee9-604b-5ffe-882a-6b81420935c4"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"9.25.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/9.25.020","content_hash":"a8e80e5b